    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Reported:** the text in the `M-x` mini-frame blends into the background and shows only where highlighted; and `ESC` / `C-g` in it blocks everything.\n\n**Likely cause of the invisible text (not confirmed):** since #115 `M-x` takes the colours `mini-frame` computes from the *frame parameters* of the parent frame. After a theme is loaded later (`sp-load-theme`) those parameters still hold the first frame's colours, while the text is drawn with the theme's `default` face. Result: a background computed from the old colours with the new text colour on it.\n\n**Change:** `sp-mini-frame--colors` reads the text colour and the background from the `default` face of the selected frame; the background is the text colour mixed in by `sp-mini-frame-contrast` (0.08, as before #115). Both are passed as frame parameters. The `M-x` prompt block uses `:inverse-video` and no colour lookup. The prompt styling hook now reports an error in the echo area instead of aborting the prompt.\n\n**Not fixed, not understood yet:** `ESC` / `C-g` blocking everything. I could not find a cause in the code; it might be input focus not returning to the main frame after the child frame is hidden, or `mini-frame-resize t` (from #119) during the exit. I have asked for details in the thread.\n\n**Not tested:** nothing was run in Emacs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
